RF.put("questb:b59",{"8699":{"id":8699,"t":"Band of Vaulted Secrets","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Magisterial Ring, 2 Azure Idols, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Windcaller Yessendra in Silithus. You must also attain Honored reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Magisterial Ring Ayamiss the Hunter 30 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ossirian the Unscarred 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , General Rajaxx 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 2 more\n2 Azure Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The rings worn by the Qiraji lieutenants are rumored to grant them formidable abilities. The corrupted gems that adorn them could, in theory, be swapped out with more pure materials to create uncorrupted versions of the rings.\nThe gems that adorn Qiraji idols would work quite well, as their quality is superior.\nBring me the ring and idols and I'll create a powerful ring for you, ‹class›.","rew":"You will receive:\nBand of Vaulted Secrets\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the ring and materials, ‹name›?","done":"I will swap the gem on the ring for you. You'll find the effect is much more... agreeable.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Windcaller Yessendra","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"92459":{"id":92459,"t":"Friend of the kirin tor","lv":33,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Archmage Celindra in the City of Dalaran.\nProvided: Arcane Mote","desc":"The council will not be happy to learn of our subterfuge, but they cannot deny results. The city is calming down, and we are free to lower our wards.\nI think it's only fair you deliver the good word. Take this mote to Archmage Celindra within the Violet Citadel.\nLevel 33 , requires level 24 Difficulty 24 29 31 36 42 Side Alliance Quest ID 92459\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 33, 10,320 XP in all.\n1 [ 33 ] An Alarming Request\nReport to the Image of Archmage Modera near the City of Dalaran.\nEmissary Jacques Hillsbrad Foothills\n650 XP\n2 [ 33 ] Heart of Disruption\nCollect the Arcane Mote for the Image of Archmage Modera near the City of Dalaran.\n9,400 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Friend of the Kirin Tor this quest\nSpeak to Archmage Celindra in the City of Dalaran.\n270 XP","cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"8299":{"id":8299,"t":"Cut Arathor Supply Lines","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Deathstalker Mortis at Hammerfall.\nArathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"The League of Arathor is sparing no expense in their move to retake Arathi. They, and all the races of the Alliance, now stream to this distant region, intent on expanding their hold from Refuge Pointe. We must stop them, and the best means to stop them is to take their supplies.\nYou can help us, ‹name›. Enter Arathi Basin, known for its rich mines, fertile land and skilled craftsman. Capture and control every base you can, win the battle, and return to me with the resources you gain.","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with The Defilers\nLevel 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable No Quest ID 8299","cats":["arathi-basin"]},"1419":{"id":1419,"t":"Coyote Thieves","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 30 Coyote Jawbones to Neeka Bloodscar in Kargath.\n30 Coyote Jawbone Feral Crag Coyote 80 % , Rabid Crag Coyote 80 % , Elder Crag Coyote 80 % , Crag Coyote 80 %","desc":"Have you spent many days in the Badlands, ‹class›? Have you felt its heat? Have you faced the beasts that wander its dusty plains? It's time you did.\nCrag coyotes are a tough breed. Tough, and bold enough to creep into Kargath and steal from our food supplies. Help rid the outpost of these thieves!\nHunt crag coyotes, ‹name›. Hunt them and bring me their jawbones. Bring me enough, and maybe I'll believe it when you say you know the Badlands.","rew":"Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Do you have the jawbones?","done":"That's a nice collection of jawbones, ‹name›. Now those coyotes won't be tearing through our supplies for scraps.\nWell done. The coyotes of the Badlands aren't easy prey. Your deed shows me that you might just survive here.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":6.5,"y":47.2,"n":"Neeka Bloodscar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"779":{"id":779,"t":"Seal of the Earth","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Diamond Runestone Scalding Whelp , Pillar of Diamond\nOpal Runestone Scalding Whelp , Pillar of Opal\nAmethyst Runestone Scalding Whelp , Scorched Guardian , Pillar of Amethyst","back":"The Seal of the Earth lies here, with three recessed alcoves for the Amethyst Runestone, the Opal Runestone, and the Diamond Runestone.","done":"As you place the Runestones into the matching recesses, a violent rumbling shakes the earth as the Seal is broken.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":81.5,"y":49.9,"n":"Seal of the Earth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"7659":{"id":7659,"t":"Imperial Plate Shoulders","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Thorium Bar","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Imperial Plate Shoulders\n+100 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"For the shoulder plans, I'll be needin' 20 thorium bars.","done":"A pleasure doin' business with ya.\nAnd ‹name›, wipe that look of disgust off yer face.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.7,"n":"Derotain Mudsipper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97899":{"id":97899,"t":"Camping 101 alchemy","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Whuut in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your alchemy skill to 20","desc":"So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.","done":"There ya have it, directions for your very own Mana Well. Most folks don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to try it out.\nNo camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those as the basis of your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. Check in with someone who can train you in cooking if you haven't already learned the basics.\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":55.8,"y":33.2,"n":"Whuut","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96059":{"id":96059,"t":"Camping 101 enchanting","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Thonys Pillarstone in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your enchanting skill to 20","desc":"Now that you've begun your journey into being an enchanter, I reckon I can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp once you've learned the ropes.\nIt's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","back":"Yes, I can teach you.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Enchanted Lute. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Ironforge","x":60.4,"y":45,"n":"Thonys Pillarstone","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94219":{"id":94219,"t":"Craftsmans writ draught of water breathing","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Draught of Water Breathing\nDraught of Water Breathing","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Draught of Water Breathing, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"If you're a customer, I got bad news for you. Some dwarf bought out the last of my stock! I'm waiting on supplies from afar now.\nIf you want empty vials though, you've come to the right place!","done":"Water breathing draughts are a necessity if you plan to camp out here during the rainy nights. I tend to take my naps under that bridge over there, but sometimes the underside gets flooded.\nNow, I can sleep easy knowing my nightmares of drowning are only just nightmares.\nCome to think of it, I probably should have ordered some to resell...","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":50.1,"y":37.7,"n":"Kixxle","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94299":{"id":94299,"t":"Craftsmans writ nightscape shoulders","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Nightscape Shoulders\nNightscape Shoulders","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Nightscape Shoulders, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Nightscape Shoulders Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94299","cats":["crafting"]},"7899":{"id":7899,"t":"Small Furry Paws","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Small Furry Paw Savannah Patriarch 59.5 % , Moonstalker 56 % , Savannah Huntress 53.8 % , Savannah Highmane 50.7 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"The first lesson in drawing a crowd is: lure them with gadgets and trinkets! Can you help me?\nI need small furry paws to use for prizes. You can find those on the cats of the Barrens or Darkshore....\nBring me some paws and I'll trade you a Darkmoon Faire ticket for them.","done":"Great, you got them! We can use these to make toys and baubles, and those will attract more people to the Faire!\nHere's your ticket, ‹name›. You earned it!\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.2,"y":69.5,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"2139":{"id":2139,"t":"Tharnariun's Hope","lv":18,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and kill the Den Mother.\nDen Mother slain","desc":"The survival of our people and lands comes at unfortunate costs, ‹name›.\nYou have spilled the blood of nature's servants; many sick animals you have felled. The people of Auberdine are indebted to you, for the forest's pain is eased--even if only for a moment.\nI have one final task for you, but be warned, you will have to kill again. It is my hope that this will be the last time I call upon you, ‹name›.\nIn a cave to the northeast, near Bashal'Aran, resides the Den Mother. Slay her.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEvergreen Gloves Timberland Cape\nExperience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","done":"You have fought for Auberdine with bravery and honor, ‹name›. In our war torn lands, death and despair are common. Many will not rise to meet the challenge of life in our new home, choosing instead to hide in their homes or escape to the more fortified lands of the Alliance.\nThank you, ‹name›. Perhaps someday soon we shall fight along side as comrades versus another foe.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":38.8,"y":43.4,"n":"Tharnariun Treetender","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"7499":{"id":7499,"t":"Codex of Defense","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,050, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Return the book to its rightful owners.\nCodex of Defense A Dusty Tome 0 % , A Dusty Tome 0 %\nProvided: Codex of Defense","desc":"The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.","rew":"You will receive:\nRoyal Seal of Eldre'Thalas\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You have recovered a tome!","done":"Excellent work, ‹race›. Should you find any more tomes, do not hesitate to return them to us.\nAs time passes, we tend to change around and even add new rewards for the return of missing tomes.\nStart an item: Codex of Defense End Lorekeeper Kildrath Level 60 , requires level 54 Difficulty 54 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Warrior Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7499","cats":["dire-maul"]},"96139":{"id":96139,"t":"The valor family","lv":22,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Search Raven Hill for anything of interest and return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire.\nRaven Hill Tome","desc":"In dark times like these, it's important we remember our heroes as much as our foes. Darkshire would not still be standing if it weren't for the bravery of folk like the good Lady Althea or those who lost their lives at Raven Hill.\nHave you read much on Raven Hill? No, of course not. Its history was wiped out along with its people. My library, impressive as it is, has little on the subject.\nIf you happen to find anything, I would appreciate bringing it here. Those folk deserve to be remembered.","rew":"You will receive:\nMemories of Valor\nExperience: 1,750","back":"Have you found anything? I'm not holding out much hope.","done":"This tome appears to be about the Valor family. I believe I've heard of a few of them. Good folk. Not sure they merit an entire book about them.\nI'll make you a copy of the tome. If you see anything else related to them on your travels, I'll be happy to take it off your hands.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.6,"y":47.6,"n":"Sirra Von'Indi","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1259":{"id":1259,"t":"Lieutenant Paval Reethe","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find out more about Reethe from Adjutant Tesoran in Theramore.","desc":"I don't recognize the name of Lieutenant Paval Reethe. Your best bet would be to check with Adjutant Tesoran. He keeps track of all the records for the Theramore guard, from personnel to their equipment.\nHe should be able to tell you who this Reethe is with a quick check of his books.","rew":"Experience: 320","done":"Hello, ‹name›. You'd like information about a specific member of the Theramore guard? Reethe, was it?\nJust give me a moment to find the right book.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68.2,"y":48.6,"n":"Captain Garran Vimes","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68,"y":48.1,"n":"Adjutant Tesoran","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"9179":{"id":9179,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Imperial Plate Chest","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 3 Imperial Plate Chests and the Craftsman's Writ - Imperial Plate Chest - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Imperial Plate Chest\n3 Imperial Plate Chest\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Imperial Plate Chest","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order BS-428:\n3 Imperial Plate Chests.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"More armor for the troops! Fantastic, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"59":{"id":59,"t":"Cloth and Leather Armor","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Sara Timberlain the Stormwind Armor Marker.\nStormwind Armor Marker\nProvided: Stormwind Armor Marker","desc":"For your shrewdness and valor, I have a marker here that is good for one piece of armor. I want you to take it to Sara Timberlain at the Eastvale Logging Camp. Give her the marker, and she will fashion the armor for you. And after you receive it, ‹name›, use it in the defense of Elwynn.\nThe Eastvale Logging Camp is beyond Guard Thomas' post to the east.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWell-stitched Robe Patched Pants\nExperience: 210\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I have been commissioned by the Stormwind Army to supply their people with cloth and leather armor.\nIf you have a marker for me, then I'd be happy to make you something.","done":"Ah, thank you for the marker. Please feel free to pick your choice of armor.\nLuck to you, brave ‹class›. And may this armor serve you well.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":65.9,"n":"Marshal Dughan","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":79.5,"y":68.8,"n":"Sara Timberlain","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"939":{"id":939,"t":"Flute of Xavaric","lv":54,"min":49,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Flute of Xavaric and 5 Jadefire Felbind samples to Eridan Bluewind in southern Felwood.\nFlute of Xavaric Xavaric\n5 Jadefire Felbind Jadefire Hellcaller 23 % , Jadefire Shadowstalker 23 % , Jadefire Felsworn 23 % , Jadefire Betrayer 23 % and 3 more\nProvided: Flute of Xavaric","desc":"You study the simple wooden flute you picked up after defeating Xavaric.\nThe knotted wood feels solid, but it seems as if the spirals and patterns in the surface begin to spin and move as you turn it over in your hands. Suddenly, you feel a sense of dread...\nYou shake your head, sure that your mind is playing tricks on you.\nIt's possible that other satyrs carry clues as to what you have found. Bring your findings to the druid, Eridan Bluewind, that lives in southern Felwood.","rew":"Experience: 5,450","back":"What is it, ‹class›? You look concerned.","done":"I sense the suffering of ancient ones, ‹name›...\nHolding these items is almost unbearable...","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.3,"y":81.5,"n":"Eridan Bluewind","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2939":{"id":2939,"t":"In Search of Knowledge","lv":47,"min":42,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to Daryn Lightwind in Rut'theran Village.","desc":"While the ruins of Feralas can be quite dangerous, they have much to tell of what has happened here.\nSearching through the rubble to the south a few days ago, I discovered what appears to be a normal stave. However, I just can't shake the feeling that there is something more to it. Angelas and I have been poring over our books here, but we can't find a thing about it.\nI have a colleague in Darnassus that may be able to tell us what this is, ‹name›. Why don't you go talk to her and see if she can help us?","rew":"Experience: 420\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Oh, so Troyas Moonbreeze sent you?\n<mutters>...always bothering me with his wild notions that he found something important...\nLook, ‹name›, I'll be blunt. Troyas always thinks he has found something important in those ruins. The truth is, anything that was truly valuable was probably hoarded away long ago by the ogres or the harpies that now reside there.\nYou're welcome to take a look around, but I don't know if you'll find any books here that will help you.\nFeralas Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":31.8,"y":45.5,"n":"Troyas Moonbreeze","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.4,"y":92.2,"n":"Daryn Lightwind","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"1579":{"id":1579,"t":"Gaffer Jacks","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Gaffer Jacks to Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine.\n8 Gaffer Jack","desc":"I came to Auberdine because of the quiet. I want to invent my inventions where it's quiet, because after a night of drinking I don't like all the noise of Ironforge!\nSo I took a ship to Auberdine and had a little too much to drink on the way. I dropped my box of gaffer jacks overboard! I need my gaffer jacks!\nI don't know exactly where I dropped them, but if you fish for them in the ocean you might get lucky...","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 460\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Did you find my gaffer jacks, ‹name›? Without my gaffer jacks I can't tune my stintle pegs!","done":"I can't believe you found them! You must be the luckiest ‹race› in Kalimdor!","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37,"y":44.1,"n":"Wizbang Cranktoggle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["fishing"]},"98059":{"id":98059,"t":"Hillsbrads hoard","lv":27,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Place the Sealed Company Request you were given on the bookkeeping table within Hillsbrad's town hall.\nSealed Company Request delivered to Hillsbrad council","desc":"Hillsbrad's council hasn't answered our new magistrate's letters. The last word I pried out of a passing merchant from the town did little to justify their silence.\nWe're only asking for a small platoon--yet I'm told multiple siege ballista rest in pristine condition within a walled-off compound.\nWalk into their town hall like a citizen returning a census request, and place this neatly upon the bookkeeping table.\nReturn to me when the deed is done.","rew":"Money: 22 0 gold, 22 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,200","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":46.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Captain McManus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"539":{"id":539,"t":"Battle of Hillsbrad","lv":28,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Foreman Bonds and 10 Hillsbrad Miners and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.\nForeman Bonds slain\nHillsbrad Miner slain : 0/ 10","desc":"The Hillsbrad Town Registry indicates that the Azureload Mine is under Alliance control. Furthermore, the mine is a prime source of iron ore for the Alliance armories.\nEven though we've struck a decisive blow to the town of Hillsbrad, the Alliance still supports and protects the Azureload Mine fervently.\nThe mine lies due south of Hillsbrad. Go there and slay the foreman, a human by the name of Bonds. Kill his miners as well. That should send a clear message to the Alliance.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"You were given direct orders to attack the Azureload Mine. Your reasons for loafing about Tarren Mill better be good or I will behead you for treason.","done":"The Dark Lady will be pleased when she learns that she has a new mine from which she can arm her soldiers.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.3,"y":20.5,"n":"High Executor Darthalia","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"1019":{"id":1019,"t":"The New Frontier","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm at the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus about the Cenarion Circle's call to explore the frontiers of Kalimdor.","desc":"Attention, heroes!\nThe Cenarion Circle seeks able bodied individuals to assist them in exploring the vast new frontiers of Kalimdor! A forbidden wasteland of unimaginable dangers lies far to the west of Tanaris and Gadgetzan, and the Circle needs willing and honorable proxies to act in their stead.\nAll interested individuals should seek audience with the Cenarion Circle. Speak with the Arch Druid in Darnassus, Fandral Staghelm, for more information!","rew":"Experience: 550","done":"What makes you think I wish to be pestered by the likes of you, ‹class›? Wait - let me stop the important duties I attend to on a daily basis so I can help you locate a doodad somewhere. By all means, the welfare of Darnassus - nay, all of Teldrassil - should come second to the acquisition of a bauble for your collection.\nThe fools in Moonglade waste my time with their call for assistance, and now I must endure this?\nDun Morogh Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.1,"y":34.2,"n":"Courier Hammerfall","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2859":{"id":2859,"t":"Wild Leather Leggings","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Turtle Scale Helms, 2 Turtle Scale Bracers, and 2 Wildvines to Jangdor Swiftstrider in Camp Mojache.\n2 Turtle Scale Helm\n2 Turtle Scale Bracers\n2 Wildvine Retherokk the Berserker 80.6 % , Zul'arek Hatefowler 65.1 % , Purple Lotus 10 % , Vilebranch Aman'zasi Guard 9.5 % and 4 more","desc":"You are ready to master more complex lessons, ‹name›. Wild Leather leggings are some of the sturdiest and powerful leather gear around. The waist, thighs, calves, and the vitals - all are given tremendous protection. Coupled with the enhancement that the wildvine provides, adventurers who own it will thank you each time they see you.\nFor you to gain this pattern, I need two Turtle Scale helms, two Turtle Scale bracers, and two wildvines.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Wild Leather Leggings\nExperience: 2,900","back":"Do you have the Turtle Scale bracers and helms ready? Don't forget the two wildvines I require.\nBy now, you're starting to realize the potential power that lies in Wild Leather armor. An armor that has no boundaries in application is nearly invaluable to a leatherworker. The limits are only in the quantities of resources to make the items - not the quality of the finished products!","done":"Again, you've completed my task without flaw. Perhaps some day I will come to YOU seeking knowledge, eh ‹name›?\nHere is the pattern for the leggings, along with my thanks. Commit this lore to your knowledge, and let your finished products tap into your impressive skills!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":42.9,"n":"Jangdor Swiftstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"1339":{"id":1339,"t":"Mountaineer Stormpike's Task","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mountaineer Stormpike.","desc":"I hear Mountaineer Stormpike is looking for a runner. Someone to do a little traveling for him. How about it? Are you the ‹race› for the job?\nIf so, then you'll find Stormpike at the top of the northern guard tower.","rew":"Experience: 550\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","done":"That's right. I have a task that I can't do while I'm guarding. In fact, it'll take you far from Loch Modan.\nYour perfect chance for adventure!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":34.2,"y":47.8,"n":"Mountaineer Kadrell","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":24.8,"y":18.4,"n":"Mountaineer Stormpike","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8619":{"id":8619,"t":"Morndeep the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...\nStart Elder Morndeep End Elder Morndeep Level 60 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 56 58 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 8619","cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9339":{"id":9339,"t":"A Thief's Reward","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 50.","rew":"You will receive:\nCrown of the Fire Festival\nExperience: 4,950","done":"You've proven yourself, today, ‹name›.\nWhile I have little else to give you, I do have this crown; a fitting gift for a conqueror. May it light your way.\nThunder Bluff Orgrimmar Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":21.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.8,"y":34.9,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.9,"y":73.1,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"9099":{"id":9099,"t":"Frostfire Sandals","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Frostfire Sandals if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Sandals, 12 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Mooncloth and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Sandals Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Gothik the Harvester 0 % in Naxxramas , Instructor Razuvious 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Mooncloth\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"As a Watcher, I was allowed access to many of Medivh's personal effects. Among those items, I found the tomes most enlightening. While the majority of the books were filled with - to put it bluntly - tripe, there were some gems. One of those tomes documented the creation of a set of armor fit for an archmage: Frostfire.\n<Angela points to her head.>\nIt's all in here and I am willing to share the fruits of that knowledge with you as long as you are able to provide me with the necessary materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostfire Sandals\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !,\nyou got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Frostfire Sandals.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"97979":{"id":97979,"t":"The goddess provides","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Cast Elune's Light and Shadowmeld.\nElune's Light cast\nShadowmeld cast","desc":"You are born kaldorei--the children of the stars--and have inherited a birthright unlike any other in this world. Elune's grace may illuminate our strengths, helping our strikes hit true, or it may help conceal us just as the moon may eclipse the sun.\nOur Long Vigil after the defense of Mount Hyjal has ended, and we have joined an Alliance of others--which you will meet in due time. For now, you are nestled in the boughs of Teldrassil.\nDemonstrate Mother Moon's gifts, and bask in her blessings.","rew":"Money: 8 0 gold, 0 silver, 8 copper Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","done":"You have seen what our goddess provides. Use it well, and she will never forsake you.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":59.2,"y":40.4,"n":"Shanda","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["night-elf"]},"93739":{"id":93739,"t":"Exploring the horde","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Nazgrel in Grommash Hold to receive further instructions. Use the instructions received to locate and speak with Vol'jin, Cairne Bloodhoof, and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.\nObtain Instructions from Nazgrel\nSpeak with Vol'jin\nSpeak with Cairne Bloodhoof\nSpeak with Lady Sylvanas Windrunner","desc":"Azeroth is a large world, and the territory of the Horde is vast. The Undercity, Orgrimmar, and Thunder Bluff all have very unique people and culture.\nIf you are to be a guest of the horde here on Azeroth, it would do you good to visit each of our capital cities in turn. Speak with my advisor Nazgrel for directions.","rew":"You will receive:\nHonorbound Cloak\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+100 reputation with Undercity\n+100 reputation with Earthen Ring\nOrgrimmar Thunder Bluff Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":32,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"9019":{"id":9019,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Devout Sandals, Devout Skirt and Devout Mantle.\nDevout Sandals Maleki the Pallid 0 % in Stratholme\nDevout Skirt Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nDevout Mantle Solakar Flamewreath 0 %\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together. Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nVirtuous Sandals Virtuous Skirt Virtuous Mantle\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, ‹name›. Let us take care of your reward first.","done":"This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.\nEastern Plaguelands Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"8939":{"id":8939,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Magister's Belt and a set of Magister's Gloves to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\nMagister's Belt Crimson Battle Mage 2.6 % , Smolderthorn Mystic 2.2 % , Crimson Sorcerer 1.9 % in Stratholme , Scholomance Adept 1.6 % in Scholomance and 3 more\nMagister's Gloves Doctor Theolen Krastinov 14 % in Scholomance , Scholomance Adept 4.6 % in Scholomance","desc":"You've proven to be a very reliable individual, ‹name›. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.\nFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.","rew":"You will receive:\nSorcerer's Belt Sorcerer's Gloves\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the exchange?","done":"Our agreement remains in place. Just remember, this is but a taste of what awaits you. Free me of this cursed fate and I will reward you with items of truly great power.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"94779":{"id":94779,"t":"Divine grace","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.","desc":"Praise be to Elune, and to your Light, ‹name›.\nAbout this time, many of our order learn abilities reflecting their faith in Elune. If knowledge serves me, I believe the same holds true for your order also.\nWhen your business in Darnassus is complete, I would seek out one of your High Priestesses for further training.\nLevel 10 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 13 16 Side Alliance Class Priest Shareable Yes Quest ID 94779","cats":["priest"]},"219":{"id":219,"t":"Missing In Action","lv":25,"min":19,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Protect Corporal Keeshan on the journey back to Redridge.","desc":"At last, friends of the Alliance!\nHelp... please...\nThe last thing I remember these foul Orcs overpowered our regiment. Most the men were killed. I took a strong blow to the head and everything went black. Now I am held captive in this cave. Help me, I am hurt badly.\nI'll need help getting back to town... please... you're my last hope...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRobe of Solomon Deputy Chain Coat Bone-studded Leather\nExperience: 2,550\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes?","done":"You have served the Kingdom well, ‹class›. Thank you for assisting Corporal Keeshan with his escape from those dreaded Blackrock Orcs. You shall be rewarded for your brave acts this day.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":23.3,"y":12.6,"n":"Corporal Keeshan","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":28.4,"y":49,"n":"Marshal Marris","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"1899":{"id":1899,"t":"The Deathstalkers","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Andron's Ledger to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter of Undercity.\nAndron's Ledger Andron's Bookshelf","desc":"You'll find the ledger with the information your employers seek on the bookshelf behind me. Deliver it with my regards, and tell them that I would prefer it if they sent you, if they find enough value that they should wish to continue our arrangement.","rew":"Experience: 230","back":"Success, ‹name›?","done":"Well, this is certainly more information than I suspected to get out of Andron. Give me a moment to peruse it, before I set you to your next task.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":54.8,"y":76.3,"n":"Andron Gant","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":83.5,"y":69.1,"n":"Mennet Carkad","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2299":{"id":2299,"t":"To Hulfdan!","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Ironforge and speak with Hulfdan Blackbeard.","desc":"Where have you been, ‹name›? Hulfdan's been looking all over the place for you. We thought the king may have put you in irons.\nGet to Ironforge as soon as possible and speak with Hulfdan!","rew":"Experience: 120","done":"Keep yer voice down, ‹name›, the guards may hear ye.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.6,"y":52.6,"n":"Hogral Bakkan","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.4,"y":23.5,"n":"Hulfdan Blackbeard","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2379":{"id":2379,"t":"Zando'zan","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Zando'zan at the Cleft of Shadow.","desc":"Your determination alone is not enough to overcome the obstacles that lay ahead of us.\nSpeak with Zando'zan to begin your training as an operative of the Shattered Hand.\nIt is only when you have mastered the practices of stealth and thievery that you may take the next step towards your destiny.","done":"Perhaps Zando'zan was wrong. Zando'zan apologizes.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":43,"y":53.7,"n":"Shenthul","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.7,"y":53,"n":"Zando'zan","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"96779":{"id":96779,"t":"Syndicate sabotage","lv":24,"min":24,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Lord Tomas inside Durnholde Keep, in Hillsbrad Foothills, and kill him. Then, return to Myrokos Silentform.\nLord Tomas slain","desc":"Sometimes, ‹race›, a single cut in the right place will drop a foe dead. The same is often true of organizations.\nOur agents have identified a key target among the ranks of the Syndicate: a man by the name of Lord Tomas.\nHe plays an instrumental role in the functions of Durnholde Keep, in Hillsbrad Foothills. If you wish to be of service to Ravenholdt, go to Durnholde and eliminate him. The quicker, and quieter, the better.","rew":"Money: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Ravenholdt\nAlterac Mountains Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":85,"y":80.4,"n":"Myrokos Silentform","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"8379":{"id":8379,"t":"Armaments of War","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Reservist's Pants Desert Bloom Gloves\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"War comes, ‹name›, and with it comes untold horrors. You have done all that could be asked of you and for that you should be rewarded.\nShould this... this prophecy ever come to pass...\n<Geologist Larksbane turns pale.>\nThe future of us all could be at an end.\nThese armaments will prove invaluable to your campaign in this desert.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"9419":{"id":9419,"t":"Scouring the Desert","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 55.","obj":"Find and deliver Silithyst to the Silithyst Extractor, then speak with Marshal Bluewall at the Alliance encampment near Hive'Zora.\nReturn Silithyst","desc":"We recently found out that the Horde has been scavenging the Silithus desert for resources, but paid them little mind. We thought it could not be worth it to station large numbers in this sweltering desert.\nHowever, it was discovered the importance of the resources, and now we are scrambling to catch up.\nIf I have your assistance, you must go into the desert and recover the silithyst and return it here.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n2 Major Healing Potion 2 Major Mana Potion\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Be careful out there, but also be quick. We have no time to lose.","done":"Thank the Light you were successful.\nNow if we could only have started this sooner, our need would not be so desperate. We must keep the bounty of the desert from falling into the hands of the Horde.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":33.3,"y":51.1,"n":"Marshal Bluewall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8779":{"id":8779,"t":"Scrying Materials","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Large Brilliant Shard, 1 Large Radiant Shard and 1 Huge Emerald to Geologist Larksbane at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing V in order to complete this quest.\nLarge Brilliant Shard\nLarge Radiant Shard\nHuge Emerald Alzzin's Minion 1.2 % , Large Obsidian Chunk 1 % , Small Obsidian Chunk 1 % , Hakkari Thorium Vein 0.9 % and 4 more\nLogistics Task Briefing V\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing V","desc":"Geologist Larksbane's studies have proven to be of tremendous value to our operations in Silithus. She has recently requested scrying materials to be used in her research.\nPlease gather these materials and deliver them to her directly so that she may continue her research.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Followup Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8859":{"id":8859,"t":"Secrets of the Colossus - Zora","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Colossus of Zora's Husk to Lord Maxwell Tyrosus at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nColossus of Zora's Husk\nProvided: Colossus of Zora's Husk","desc":"My servants were nearly killed in their efforts to recover this sample. You absolutely must hurry! Lord Maxwell Tyrosus eagerly awaits a fresh husk sample. He believes that the secrets of this Colossus could help us in the war against the Scourge!\nWhy are you still here!? To Light's Hope! Yes, you will be rewarded handsomely for your efforts...","rew":"You will receive:\nColossal Bag of Loot\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You look a bit heavy in the boots, friend.","done":"Excellent and timely! Well done, lad/lass.\nSilithus Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.5,"y":37.4,"n":"Colossus Researcher Sophia","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.9,"y":48.4,"n":"Lord Maxwell Tyrosus","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8539":{"id":8539,"t":"Target: Hive'Zora Hive Sisters","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 30 Hive'Zora Hive Sisters and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Combat Task Briefing V in order to complete this quest.\nCombat Task Briefing V\nHive'Zora Hive Sister slain : 0/ 30\nProvided: Combat Task Briefing V","desc":"Reinforcements have been called on to join the assault on Hive'Zora. You have been selected to target Hive'Zora hive sisters. Report back to Commander Mar'alith after completing your task.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Combat Badge\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something to tell me, ‹class›?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. You're a worthy ally.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"98299":{"id":98299,"t":"Stop the spread","lv":20,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 5 Sickly Refugees and 5 Haggard Refugees for Dalar Dawnweaver in The Sepulcher.\nHaggard Refugee slain : 0/ 5\nSickly Refugee slain : 0/ 5","desc":"If there is one thing we do know, it is that Arugal is responsible for worgen within Silverpine--be it his own machinations or otherwise. What we don't know is how it spreads.\nWhile I research a way to stop the curse, our first priority is to contain it. It appears this affliction cannot infect forsaken, but a large group of humans have gathered by the Greymane Wall.\nGo to the wall and put down these refugees before they have a chance to become servants for Arugal. And try not to get bit, ‹race›.","rew":"Money: 12 0 gold, 12 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Undercity","done":"It seems the Gilneans are not too keen on allowing anyone past their wall. That is fortunate, I suppose. It means there is likely no chance for the worgen curse to spread to their city.\nCan you imagine the depravity if an entire kingdom were infected?","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44.2,"y":39.8,"n":"Dalar Dawnweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"98219":{"id":98219,"t":"The shamed lieutenant","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore in Hillsbrad Foothills.","desc":"Thank you again for delivering the statuette safely, ‹name›.\nI could use your help with something else. There's a member of the city guard who was reassigned to duty in Southshore out in the Hillsbrad Foothills.\nHis father was a friend of mine, and while I don't disagree that he could use the lesson... I'd still like to see him succeed. He would really benefit from someone like you helping him out.\nThere is a boat that can take you that way from Menethil Harbor, if you are passing back through.\nStormwind City Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.2,"y":33,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.4,"y":58.4,"n":"Lieutenant Farren Orinelle","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"619":{"id":619,"t":"Enticing Negolash","lv":52,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Barbecued Buzzard Wing\n5 Junglevine Wine Stomper Kreeg 23 % , sold by Nixxrax Fillamug","back":"This is an abandoned lifeboat. Printed along its side in scratched, faded paint are the words:\n\"Smotts' Revenge\"","done":"You pile food and drink upon the raft...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.5,"y":82,"n":"Ruined Lifeboat","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8059":{"id":8059,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Demoniac's Wraps","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Stanchion. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.\nAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Stanchion\nReach 3000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"Warlocks tread dangerous ground in dealing with demons, but our demoniacs take this one step further. Through an ancient and arcane ritual, they allow a demon to enter their being. Rather than let it possess them though, they enslave the demon from the inside, absorbing the power of the beast for their own command. It is a feat few are ever able to master.\nFor you to learn of the power of the demoniac, I must have Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub. Go there and retrieve that which we seek.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Demoniac's Wraps\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Have you returned with the Paragons of Power? By defeating the diabolic minions of the Hakkar, you will not only prove yourself to us, but also your willingness to learn the ways of the demoniac.","done":"Well done... no doubt they were made to pay in excruciating ways before they gave up the Paragons of Power. Take this - the demoniac's wraps. Made from powerful mojo used in summoning the demoniac's prey, it is a powerful tool in your acquisition of power.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"9259":{"id":9259,"t":"Traitor to the Bloodsail","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"40 Silk Cloth Protector Weaver , Mountaineer Langarr 85.7 % , Watcher Wollpert 85.7 % , Mountaineer Zwarn 78.3 % and 4 more\n4 Red Dye sold by Tharynn Bouden , sold by Gina MacGregor , sold by Banalash , sold by Nerrist and 4 more","back":"That mangy dog, Revilgaz, has offered to pardon any former Bloodsails willing to turn on their cap'n! That bilge sucker asked me to go an' off me ole' mates and to bring back their bandannas as proof.\nI don't have it in me heart to do that, nor will I ask ye to. Bring me some silk cloth and red dye and I'll make suitable replicas. I'll tell the Baron you went turncoat, but be warned... the Bloodsails are not gonna like it!","done":"Let us observe a minute of silence for our fallen mates, ‹name›.\n<The Bloodsail Traitor grins at you and winks.>\nBeing a traitor is one thing, murdering yer own buckos... that'd be just downright despicable, aye!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":31.8,"y":70.9,"n":"Bloodsail Traitor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"699":{"id":699,"t":"Lack of Surplus","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Sawtooth Snapper Claws to Tok'Kar in the Swamp of Sorrows.\n6 Sawtooth Snapper Claw Sawtooth Snapper 80 %","desc":"With the threat of murlocs along the coast, we're stationed out here to protect--or warn if the force is too large--of any coming threats to Stonard. It doesn't give us much time for relaxation, and we could use some more help if you're able.\nThe sawtooth snappers' claws make for fine weapons when properly prepared. Bring me some of their claws and I'll see you're rewarded with one of our weapons in thanks for the fresh meat and the good company.","rew":"Experience: 3,450\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Good mead, a warm fire, an army of orcs and an arsenal of weapons... that's all we really need out here along the coast. I don't regret my position out here safeguarding Stonard, but it would be nice if we could one day get a burrow, or at least a tower.","done":"Glad to see you're alive and well, ‹name›.\nThese claws should make do nicely. The more weapons we have at the ready for attacks against us, the better off we'll be.\nI'll get started on your weapon as soon as possible. It will only take a short time. I've become quite adept and quick at their production.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":81.3,"y":81,"n":"Tok'Kar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"379":{"id":379,"t":"Slake That Thirst","lv":46,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Wastewander Water Pouches to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan.\n5 Wastewander Water Pouch Andre Firebeard 35 % , Wastewander Scofflaw 35 % , Wastewander Assassin 35 % , Wastewander Bandit 35 % and 3 more","desc":"You want a power source. I can help you with that. Know what I want? I want something to drink! Bring me five Wastewander Water Pouches, and I'll give you the 4711-FTZ.\nNow... guess where you can find Wastewander Water Pouches! Why don't you walk up to one of the Wastewander nomads to the east of here and ask them for one. Let me know how that works out for you.","rew":"You will receive:\nModel 4711-FTZ Power Source\nExperience: 3,050\n+75 reputation with Undercity\n+75 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Well, did the nomads 'volunteer' up those water pouches for you?","done":"Excellent, the power source is yours. Now, it isn't completely designed for use in a science kit like that, so you'll only have a limited amount of time before all the data you collect will go kablooey!\nWhen you collect everything you need for whatever it is you are doing, bring it to me and I'll shut it down properly. You'll have at most two hours to get what you need to get done, done.\nIf you don't get it done in time, I can always sell you another power source to try again. You heard me - sell!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":28.5,"n":"Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"459":{"id":459,"t":"The Woodland Protector","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 8 Fel Moss and bring them to Tarindrella.\n8 Fel Moss Grellkin 80 % , Grell 80 %","desc":"Something evil is brewing in the forests of Teldrassil. Look long the hills to where the peaceful furbolgs used to dwell. They have deserted their homes and are amassing under the name of the Gnarlpine tribe.\nOnly the corruption of wicked Fel Moss could cause such a transformation. The grells and grellkin have infested the area and are threatening the residents of Shadowglen.\nEngage these grells and grellkin, ‹name›, and see if they are indeed caught under the enchantment of the wicked Fel Moss.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCanopy Leggings Tracking Boots Viny Gloves\nYou will also receive:\n3 Healing Herb\nExperience: 250\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Satisfy my suspicions, ‹name›. Bring to me 8 Fel Moss.","done":"Your service to the creatures of Shadowglen is worthy of reward, ‹name›.\nYou confirmed my fears, however. If the grells have become tainted by the Fel Moss, one can only imagine what has become of the Gnarlpine tribe of furbolgs who once lived here.\nShould you find yourself in Dolanaar, able ‹class›, seek out the knowledgeable druid, Athridas Bearmantle. He shares our concern for the well being of the forest.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.8,"y":45.2,"n":"Tarindrella","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"2459":{"id":2459,"t":"Ferocitas the Dream Eater","lv":8,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar wants you to kill 7 Gnarlpine Mystics and find the Missing Jewel.\nTallonkai's Jewel\nGnarlpine Mystic slain : 0/ 7","desc":"The emerald... It is missing! My dreamcatcher has been damaged!\nThere is a band of Gnarlpine mystics located to the north of Starbreeze. I have heard reports that their leader, Ferocitas the Dream Eater has been wearing a necklace that glows green in the night. Now seeing my dreamcatcher, I am sure that he has stolen my emerald... He would never realize that its power is useless to him.\nFind this missing jewel, ‹name›. And, while you're there, clear out some of the corrupted mystics as well.","rew":"Money: 4 50 0 gold, 4 silver, 50 copper Experience: 875\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Ferocitas and the Gnarlpine Mystics must return what is mine. Please retrieve the emerald so that I may repair my emerald dreamcatcher.","done":"Now I can repair my dreamcatcher. Thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.6,"y":56.9,"n":"Tallonkai Swiftroot","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"95819":{"id":95819,"t":"Sign me up","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the completed form to Jornah in The Barrens.\nAdvertising License Application\nMassive Pile of Completed Forms","desc":"Greetings, accomplished craftsperson!\nCompletion of this form will grant you non-exclusive, revocable, and legally limited permission to display advertisement signs for your tradeskill(s) all across Azeroth!\nOnce completed, please bring this to your local Durotar Supply & Logistics Contract Coordinator to begin processing.\nHappy crafting!","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650\nStart an item: Advertising License Application Level 60 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 56 58 Side Both factions Quest ID 95819","cats":["the-barrens"]},"1099":{"id":1099,"t":"Goblins win","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Goblin Race Ticket","rew":"You will receive:\nGoblin Prize Box\nLevel 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 1099","cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1179":{"id":1179,"t":"The Brassbolts Brothers","lv":30,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the crate of crash helmets to Wizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats.\nCrate of Crash Helmets\nProvided: Crate of Crash Helmets","desc":"You ever heard of the Shimmering Flats? It's a stretch of salt flats way over in Kalimdor, just south of the Thousand Needles canyon. It's a great place for racing because, well, it's so flat!\nA couple of gnome brothers are out there, friends of mine, trying out their new rocket car, and from what I hear it's fast! Heh, so fast that their pilots keep crashing. Giving themselves concussions.\nSo they asked me for some Siege Engine helmets, but I have duties here. I can't make the trip!\nCan you?","rew":"Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Watch where you're stepping! Watch watch watch!! This is delicate stuff you see here, and if we're to win then it must all work perfectly!","done":"Ah! Longbeard sent you with a load of helmets! Hooray!\nNow maybe we can talk a pilot into driving our car...\nDun Morogh Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.8,"y":36.2,"n":"Pilot Longbeard","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.1,"y":77.1,"n":"Wizzle Brassbolts","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"7819":{"id":7819,"t":"Additional Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","back":"Greetings once again, ‹name›! Our need for runecloth is constant, and we can always use additional resources if you are willing to part with them. For an additional stack of twenty runecloth, I will make sure that you are recognized for your continuing efforts on behalf of the Undercity.\nWhenever you are ready to hand in the stack of runecloth, I'll accept it.","done":"‹name› - without heroes like you working on behalf of the Forsaken, we'd surely suffer. Thank you for your continued efforts!","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":71.7,"y":29.2,"n":"Ralston Farnsley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"3099":{"id":3099,"t":"Tainted Scroll","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Tainted Scroll and speak to Maximillion in Deathknell.\nTainted Scroll\nProvided: Tainted Scroll","desc":"Ah, while you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. I would think it's some matter of importance as it seems it bears the seal of the warlock trainer Maximillion. I would take some time to read it before heading out again.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"I bid you welcome, brother/sister. I knew you would come. It was only a matter of time.\nWhat I said interested you, didn't it? I hit a chord... something inside you knew what I claimed was truth. Good.\nKnow this though: I am no traitor to Sylvanas. If anything, she would appreciate my claims considering it was her own beliefs that has put the Forsaken in the position it is now.","done":"I mentioned a slave still being a slave, no matter the master. Do you remember? We both know that it is that type of control--that type of power--that now drives us. We seek to have creatures serve us. We know we are more powerful and deserve more respect than others give us ... and so now we look to take it.\nI will be your ally in this struggle--the struggle for our own freedom. Freedom to seek our own allegiances. When you feel ready, return to me and I will teach you all I know.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.8,"y":66.2,"n":"Shadow Priest Sarvis","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.9,"y":66.3,"n":"Maximillion","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1499":{"id":1499,"t":"Vile Familiars","lv":4,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Zureetha Fargaze.","desc":"Zureetha has been sending novices like yourself to help cull the numbers of the creatures in the cave near where you fought the vile familiars.\nI think it would be good for you to gain experience by assisting her. Be sure to tell her that you assisted with the imp problem, she'll probably have a reward for you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPrimitive Hand Blade Primitive Walking Stick\nExperience: 35\n+10 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+10 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"You have done well, ‹name›.\nAlthough the vile familiars were merely pets of the darker powers within the Burning Blade, your success against them foretells greater deeds ahead.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.6,"y":69,"n":"Ruzan","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.8,"y":69.1,"n":"Zureetha Fargaze","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1739":{"id":1739,"t":"The Binding","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Using the Heartswood Core, summon and subdue a succubus, then return the Heartswood Core to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Slaughtered Lamb.\nSummoned Succubus slain\nProvided: Heartswood Core","desc":"Using the heartswood core, you will be able to cast a spell at the summoning circle in the crypt below to open a portal for the succubus to pass through.\nBe careful, ‹name›, succubi have overrun even the strongest of minds.\nOnce you have bested and returned it to the void, return to me and I will show you how to call and control it.","rew":"You will receive:\nSmall Soul Pouch\nYou will learn: Summon Succubus\nExperience: 1,150","back":"Sometimes I wonder if Surena was not a succubus in disguise, sent to warp and twist my mind... Ha! I give her too much credit, I think.","done":"Well done, well done, ‹name›. I see we've done right in deciding to train you. Your performance certainly does not disappoint.\nI've no qualms in showing you the way to control your newly bound succubus. Observe carefully.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85.2,"n":"Gakin the Darkbinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1819":{"id":1819,"t":"Ulag the Cleaver","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Ulag the Cleaver, then speak with Deathguard Dillinger.\nUlag the Cleaver slain","desc":"When the Scourge swept through Tirisfal Glades, we captured one to study. He had a free mind, and called himself Ulag the Cleaver. But, although his will was free, he was still enthralled by the Lich King.\nWe hoped to find a way to break the king's control over Ulag, but we failed. Now, finally, it is time to free him.\nFree him, and kill him.\nActivate the skull stone trigger near the mausoleum to the north. This will lift the magical seal that binds him.\nThen... be ready, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 850","back":"Your task is yet undone, ‹name›. It is not wise for a warrior to show fear...","done":"Well done, ‹name›. Ulag was no minor agent of the Scourge. You have shown the Deathguards, and hence the Dark Lady, that you are a warrior of skill and resolve, and are worthy of further instruction.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":58.2,"y":51.4,"n":"Deathguard Dillinger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"139":{"id":139,"t":"Captain Sander's Hidden Treasure","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search the empty jug next to the windmill for the next clue.\nProvided: Another Clue to Sander's Treasure","desc":"Searching through the barrel you discover another piece of parchment. This one reads: Now from this here barrel, face ye North. Straight as the crow flies, keep ye walkin' till you see the empty jug next to the lone windmill on the sea bluffs. If ye poke around that jug, ye just might find what you're lookin' for.","rew":"Experience: 575","done":"You're on your way to the jackpot, treasure seeker!","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":40.5,"y":47.8,"n":"Broken Barrel","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":40.6,"y":17,"n":"Old Jug","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"98459":{"id":98459,"t":"A lack of virtue","lv":21,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver Tom's Gift to Bart Tidewater in Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.\nProvided: Tom's Gift","desc":"Bart Tidewater's a no-good cheapskate, I tell ya!\n\"Captain of the Maiden's Virtue\" he calls himself. That ship's sailed as far as a rock in Tanaris! He's no captain, he's an actor who won enough hands of poker to buy the Virtue in the first place!\nIf you ever find yourself in Menethil Harbor over in the Wetlands, give this to him and let him know it's from ol' Half-fish.\nThere's a boat from here that can take you right to the harbor, by the way. It'll be the second stop!\nAnd he cheats at poker!","back":"Put yer backs into it! We set sail on my word!\nOh? What's that you have there, traveler?","done":"<Bart unwraps the gift.>\nWhy that no good, son of a--\nDid he even tell you that HE is the one who cheats at poker?! I only won enough money to buy the Maiden's Virtue after we kicked him out of our poker circle!\nI swear, the next time I see that absolute waste of seawater--\nI'm sorry, I'm sorry. I shouldn't shoot the messenger. On behalf of the crew of the Maiden's Virtue--finest ship in the Great Sea--welcome to Menethil Harbor!\nHillsbrad Foothills Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.2,"y":66.4,"n":"Tom \"Half-fish\" Wilson","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":8.8,"y":59.8,"n":"Bart Tidewater","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"299":{"id":299,"t":"Uncovering the Past","lv":27,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 27 instead of 28. Requires level 22 instead of 25. Pays 22s instead of 25s. Gives 2,200 experience instead of 2,300, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Prospector Whelgar wants you to scour the excavation site in search of the 4 missing tablet fragments: Ados, Modr, Golm and Neru.\nAdos Fragment Ancient Relic\nModr Fragment Ancient Relic\nGolm Fragment Ancient Relic\nNeru Fragment Loose Soil","desc":"Just before the invasion I uncovered a large tablet called the Goaz Stone. The translated text breaks off in 4 places. The text speaks of a \"divine plan\" and a \"doomed prophecy.\"\nI fear we are running out of time. I am too old to go down and brave those beasts. But you are strong.\nScour the excavation site and uncover the 4 missing tablet fragments: Ados, Modr, Golm and Neru. Search for them in ancient artifacts or where the soil is loose. Bring them to me so I can begin unlocking the mystery!","rew":"You will receive:\nSilk Mantle of Gamn\nMoney: 22 0 gold, 22 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,200\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Have you uncovered the four fragments yet, ‹name›? Ados, Modr, Golm and Neru...","done":"Ah the Goaz Stone is complete! Fine work, ‹name›. Fine work indeed. Now I can continue with the delicate translation of this Titan script. I can make out new words already! Hmm. . .it says here, \"Old Gods. . .Chained Beneath the Land.\" This is the beginning of something epic.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":38.8,"y":52.4,"n":"Prospector Whelgar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92699":{"id":92699,"t":"The supreme magister","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Elaadrin Evengale in Valanaar.","desc":"Now that you've arrived in Valanaar, you'll likely want to check in with the other members of the High Order here. The current Supreme Magister, Elaadrin Evengale and his people operate out of the lodge on the far southeastern part of Valanaar.\nYou should also take care, the High Order and Windshapers don't get along very well here. Be careful and give the Windshapers a good, wide berth. We've got enough to worry about with the cult, I won't tolerate faction violence in the streets of Valanaar.","done":"Hello and welcome. Rathiril sent me a magical missive about you and he mentioned you had some promise.\nWith you standing before me now, I can see why he suggested you seek me out. You have a vibrant arcane aura about you. Few enough of us anymore have the aptitude, let alone the will, to do what is needed to save our home. Do you have the boldness and strength needed to aid The High Order?\nI suppose we will see.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.6,"y":79.8,"n":"Elaadrin Evengale","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});